# iris, forked because two defects upstream has not fixed make it unpleasant to live with.
#
# The shell autocomplete. It is built rather than installed, and each fix sits on its own
# branch one series above upstream, so either can be offered back without being rewritten
# first. decisions/shell-autocomplete.md carries why it is here at all, including the half day
# it was disabled so the agents panel could see through it, and what it costs.
name      | iris
upstream  | https://github.com/versenilvis/IRIS.git
fork      | https://github.com/milosdjakovic/IRIS.git
base      | v0.7.0
pin       | b8b7ac8bf801eb8a0ca47db2d1c93aa1337bc9b9
dest      | .local/bin/iris
decisions | decisions/shell-autocomplete.md

# Upstream tags a nightly for almost every commit, and a nightly is not a thing anyone here
# decides about, so the releases worth reporting are named rather than left to the default.
releases         | v[0-9]*
releases-exclude | *nightly*

patch | fix/alias-display-preserves-typed-command | a suggestion reads back the alias target instead of the word that was typed, so with cd aliased to zoxide every row reads z and the ghost text dies with it | https://github.com/versenilvis/IRIS/issues/158
patch | feat/appearance-aware-theme               | a theme carrying a half per terminal appearance, which upstream has no notion of, so its selection bar cannot be a tint of the page it sits on | 

watch | https://github.com/versenilvis/IRIS/issues/158 | open | the alias display bug, the one patch here that upstream has a report for
